cff-version: 1.2.0
# TODO(team): replace the placeholder author list with the six group members
# before submission. Add `orcid:` and `affiliation:` where you have them.
title: RoadAnomaly — pixel-level road anomaly detection
abstract: >-
  Comparative study of anomaly segmentation on the RoadAnomaly benchmark:
  autoencoder reconstruction error, image resynthesis (Lis et al., ICCV 2019)
  and transfer-learned segmentation, served through a FastAPI inference
  service with a Next.js dashboard.
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite it and the RoadAnomaly dataset paper
  listed under references.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/adriansalvadorekomo/RoadAnomaly
keywords:
  - anomaly detection
  - semantic segmentation
  - road scenes
  - autonomous driving
  - deep learning
authors:
  - alias: adriansalvadorekomo
    # TODO(team): add the remaining five members here
    given-names: Adrian
    family-names: Salvatore
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: Detecting the Unexpected via Image Resynthesis
    year: 2019
    authors:
      - family-names: Lis
        given-names: Krzysztof
      - family-names: Nakka
        given-names: Krishna
      - family-names: Fua
        given-names: Pascal
      - family-names: Salzmann
        given-names: Mathieu
    conference:
      name: International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV)
    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.07595
notes: >-
  The repository code is MIT licensed. The bundled dataset is not: see LICENSE
  and data/credits.txt for per-image attribution and the CC BY-SA 4.0 terms
  that apply to the annotations.
